{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W9uBoa79y3iaWtbVaWzJV9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details for CoRL 2026 don't appear to be fully available yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics conference (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Resources\n\nFor more detailed reviewer guidelines, you may want to check:\n- The **CoRL 2026 OpenReview page** (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference) - where reviewer details and the review form are likely to be posted\n- **Past CoRL reviewer guidelines** - The search found CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines that provide insight into the review evaluation criteria and process\n\nThe most comprehensive and up-to-date reviewer guidelines and review forms for CoRL 2026 would likely be available directly on the OpenReview platform or the CoRL 2026 official website.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31fb0b7f-0c9b-4a80-b3d9-4c267606ceee","uuid":"c8c56106-a841-4aa7-b46f-34e59309f2c5","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:42:58.040Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0188eugFjq9Qd2MsAiKxMewC","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details for CoRL 2026 don't appear to be fully available yet. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics conference (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Related Resources\n\nFor more detailed reviewer guidelines, you may want to check:\n- The **CoRL 2026 OpenReview page** (https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference) - where reviewer details and the review form are likely to be posted\n- **Past CoRL reviewer guidelines** - The search found CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines that provide insight into the review evaluation criteria and process\n\nThe most comprehensive and up-to-date reviewer guidelines and review forms for CoRL 2026 would likely be available directly on the OpenReview platform or the CoRL 2026 official website."],"durationSeconds":6.097239014000002}}
