{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGtCdHTu5biZ4EvqcpuAfE","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form Extraction\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot extract a complete review form with the requested details.\n\n## What IS Present:\n\nThe document outlines **review criteria** for regular papers:\n- \"Evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- Assessment of \"degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- Relevance to robotic learning is required\n\n## What IS NOT Present:\n\n- **No scoring scale** (1-10, letter grades, or similar)\n- **No score level descriptions** (e.g., what constitutes \"excellent\" vs. \"weak\")\n- **No complete review form structure** with evaluation dimensions\n- **No acceptance rate** mentioned\n- **No explicit accept/reject guidance** for reviewers\n\n## Additional Content:\n\nThe page does include desk rejection criteria (formatting, anonymity, scope violations) and reviewer qualification standards, but these are separate from the actual review evaluation form.\n\n**Conclusion:** This page appears to be instructional guidance rather than the complete formal review template reviewers would use during evaluation."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31fb0b7f-0c9b-4a80-b3d9-4c267606ceee","uuid":"3875c998-2138-45a5-bfae-b96d3a6ddb2d","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:43:07.041Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":134101,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form Extraction\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot extract a complete review form with the requested details.\n\n## What IS Present:\n\nThe document outlines **review criteria** for regular papers:\n- \"Evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- Assessment of \"degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- Relevance to robotic learning is required\n\n## What IS NOT Present:\n\n- **No scoring scale** (1-10, letter grades, or similar)\n- **No score level descriptions** (e.g., what constitutes \"excellent\" vs. \"weak\")\n- **No complete review form structure** with evaluation dimensions\n- **No acceptance rate** mentioned\n- **No explicit accept/reject guidance** for reviewers\n\n## Additional Content:\n\nThe page does include desk rejection criteria (formatting, anonymity, scope violations) and reviewer qualification standards, but these are separate from the actual review evaluation form.\n\n**Conclusion:** This page appears to be instructional guidance rather than the complete formal review template reviewers would use during evaluation.","durationMs":3695,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014DT6gdQtCe7TfxVLdkQKQn","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided content, I can identify the evaluation dimensions but cannot extract a complete review form with scoring scales, as this information is not fully detailed in the document.\n\n## Identified Evaluation Dimensions\n\nThe guidelines specify reviewers should evaluate papers on six criteria:\n\n1. **Originality** - novelty of problems/methods and differentiation from prior work\n2. **Quality** - technical soundness and adequate substantiation of claims\n3. **Clarity** - writing quality and organization\n4. **Significance** - importance and potential impact on the field\n5. **Relevance** - alignment with robot learning focus and CoRL audience interest\n6. **Limitations** - quality of authors' self-assessment of shortcomings\n\n## Missing Information\n\nThe document does not provide:\n- Specific scoring scale (e.g., 1-10, accept/reject thresholds)\n- Detailed descriptions of each score level\n- Explicit acceptance/reject guidance\n- Acceptance rate statistics\n\n## Key Guidance\n\nThe guidelines emphasize constructive feedback and list common reviewer mistakes to avoid, referencing \"ICML\" and \"NeurIPS\" resources for additional direction. However, the actual numerical scoring mechanism and decision criteria are not included in this excerpt."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31fb0b7f-0c9b-4a80-b3d9-4c267606ceee","uuid":"d9e8c4aa-0233-4be4-9ca2-bc4cfc576396","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:43:08.258Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided content, I can identify the evaluation dimensions but cannot extract a complete review form with scoring scales, as this information is not fully detailed in the document.\n\n## Identified Evaluation Dimensions\n\nThe guidelines specify reviewers should evaluate papers on six criteria:\n\n1. **Originality** - novelty of problems/methods and differentiation from prior work\n2. **Quality** - technical soundness and adequate substantiation of claims\n3. **Clarity** - writing quality and organization\n4. **Significance** - importance and potential impact on the field\n5. **Relevance** - alignment with robot learning focus and CoRL audience interest\n6. **Limitations** - quality of authors' self-assessment of shortcomings\n\n## Missing Information\n\nThe document does not provide:\n- Specific scoring scale (e.g., 1-10, accept/reject thresholds)\n- Detailed descriptions of each score level\n- Explicit acceptance/reject guidance\n- Acceptance rate statistics\n\n## Key Guidance\n\nThe guidelines emphasize constructive feedback and list common reviewer mistakes to avoid, referencing \"ICML\" and \"NeurIPS\" resources for additional direction. However, the actual numerical scoring mechanism and decision criteria are not included in this excerpt.","durationMs":3960,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
