{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M5nyGj1mF2mPV79RDys4gT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL OpenReview review form \"overall score\" rating scale 1 10\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process\"},{\"title\":\"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137\"},{\"title\":\"OpenReview Should be Protected and Leveraged as a Community Asset for Research in the Era of Large Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.21537\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenReview's rating scale, though the results show the default OpenReview form rather than CoRL-specific details.\n\nThe OpenReview default review form uses a 1-10 rating scale with the following descriptions: 10 for \"Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\", 9 for \"Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\", 8 for \"Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\", 7 for \"Good paper, accept\", 6 for \"Marginally above acceptance threshold\", 5 for \"Marginally below acceptance threshold\", 4 for \"Ok but not good enough - rejection\", 3 for \"Clear rejection\", 2 for \"Strong rejection\", and 1 for \"Trivial or wrong\".\n\nThe CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines mention the review form structure but don't provide the specific overall score rating scale in the excerpt that was returned. If you need CoRL-specific rating scale information, you may want to check the official CoRL guidelines or reviewer instructions directl